5701: \subsection{Command-run boundary}
5702: 
5703: \begin{proposition}[Command-run boundary inventory]
5704: \label{audit:command-run-boundary-inventory}
5705: For the current presentation package, Table~\ref{tab:command-boundary-inventory}
5706: is complete for the command-boundary claims used by
5707: Proposition~\ref{prop:machine-readable-certificate-records},
5708: Proposition~\ref{audit:review-bundle-availability-condition}, and
5709: the finite-record interface theorem, Theorem~\ref{thm:publication-safety-interface}.  The accepted fresh command-run
5710: claims in the package are exactly the three finite record-verifier invocations
5711: recorded in \path{review_bundle/certificate_verification_run.log} and
5712: \path{review_bundle/source_interface_verification_run.log}, and
5713: \path{review_bundle/primary_claim_inventory_freshness_2026-06-05.log}, together
5714: with the live venue and bibliography freshness check recorded in
5715: \path{review_bundle/VENUE_BIBLIOGRAPHY_LIVE_CHECK_2026-06-06_ROUND5.log}.  The
5716: Lean/BEDC source theorem semantics, publication-daemon or route-state surfaces,
5717: and Rule110/\allowbreak GroundCompiler artifact surfaces remain path-verified,
5718: historical, or bounded-artifact evidence and are not command-run validation
5719: claims.
5720: \end{proposition}
5721: 
5722: 
5723: \medskip
5724: \begin{proof}
5725: The evidence-level definition in
5726: Definition~\ref{def:operational-acceptance-interface} requires a command-run row
5727: to record command, immutable source state, environment, exit code, and log
5728: path; otherwise the boundary field must say that no command-run assertion is
5729: made.  The first four rows of Table~\ref{tab:command-boundary-inventory} contain
5730: all five required command-run fields.  The first log records command
5731: \path{python review_bundle/verify_certificate_records.py}, source state
5732: \path{automath repository commit 305ee93353b16babc461bfad1a7aee9c808ee268 plus review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md},
5733: \path{Python 3.10.11 on Windows 10}, exit code \path{0}, and log path
5734: \path{review_bundle/certificate_verification_run.log}.  Its negative boundary is
5735: schema-level certificate-record verification only, with no Lean, daemon, or
5736: Rule110 rerun.  The second log records command
5737: \path{python review_bundle/verify_source_interface_record.py}, the same source
5738: state and Python environment, exit code \path{0}, and log path
5739: \path{review_bundle/source_interface_verification_run.log}.  Its negative
5740: boundary is finite source-record comparison only: it compares table rows, JSON
5741: records, manifest ranges, labels, digest, and line count, without validating the
5742: external theorem semantics.  The third log records command
5743: \path{python review_bundle/verify_primary_claim_inventory.py}, the same source
5744: state and Python environment, exit code \path{0}, and log path
5745: \path{review_bundle/primary_claim_inventory_freshness_2026-06-05.log}.  Its
5746: negative boundary is finite primary-inventory freshness only: it checks source
5747: line spans, row shape, the \path{pc1}--\path{pc12} row id set, and
5748: certificate-like pointers, without proving the semantics of the primary prose.
5749: The fourth log records command \path{PowerShell Invoke-WebRequest against CICM
5750: route pages and bibliography authority pages}, source state
5751: \path{main.tex, submission_abstract.tex, references.bib, and review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md at 2026-06-06 Stage A2 theoremization round 5 packaging},
5752: environment \path{Windows PowerShell 5.1 on Windows; network enabled}, exit code
5753: \path{0}, and log path
5754: \path{review_bundle/VENUE_BIBLIOGRAPHY_LIVE_CHECK_2026-06-06_ROUND5.log}.  Its negative
5755: boundary is live route and bibliography freshness only: it confirms reachability
5756: of the CICM presentation-only call, EasyChair/LNCS interface pages, DOI or arXiv
5757: locators, and the public source repository on 2026-06-06 local date, without certifying
5758: venue acceptance, venue upload, archive minting, Lean rebuilds, or artifact
5759: reruns.
5760: 
5761: The remaining three rows have no command field, no environment field, no exit
5762: code, and no rerun log.  Their accepted surfaces are instead the bounded source
5763: theorem interface at the pinned commit, the route and case-witness tables, and
5764: the bounded artifact certificate $a_6$ with its manifest and review-bundle
5765: snapshots.  Those are precisely the evidence surfaces used in the cited
5766: propositions and in the finite certificate-construction theorem.  By the verifier rule, a row
5767: lacking command-run fields can only be accepted at its declared path-verified,
5768: historical, or bounded-artifact level.  Thus the table exhausts the
5769: command-boundary inventory and prevents the non-rerun Lean, daemon, Rule110, and
5770: external source-theorem semantics surfaces from being promoted by prose into
5771: fresh execution claims.
5772: \end{proof}
5773: 
5774: This long technical supplement reports path-verified source architecture and case evidence.
5775: It does not claim a fresh rebuild of the full newmath source tree.  A command-run
5776: claim is outside the present evidence level unless the source commit,
5777: environment, command, exit code, and log path are recorded with the submission.
5778: This boundary is deliberate: the workflow is meant to make unsupported claims
5779: visible rather than to hide them behind generated prose.
5780: 
5781: For the current presentation-only submission route, the public source link is
5782: the newmath repository \cite{bedc-newmath-source} at pinned commit
5783: \path{3fb3d6a0641767388a401883062aa522ea0b397b}.  The automath workspace record
5784: and the review-bundle record are treated as submission-local support notes, not
5785: ordinary external bibliography items.  They provide extracted line-range records,
5786: case-evidence manifests, submission-local provenance, and the technical
5787: supplement only when uploaded exactly with the submission and matching final
5788: digests, as required by
5789: Proposition~\ref{audit:review-bundle-availability-condition}.
5790: No DOI, institutional archive, dynamic validation service, or fresh command-run
5791: evidence is claimed here; the bundle-dependent evidence claim is conditional on
5792: that supplemental surface being available to reviewers.
5793: 
5794: \section{Conclusion and support-boundary summary}
5795: 
5796: The supplement's theorem chain proves a finite-record certificate calculus for
5797: publication claims under record-gate soundness.  The core mathematical/software
5798: claim is not that AI output is proof evidence, that the workflow is a theorem
5799: prover, that all BEDC declarations have been freshly rebuilt, or that the Rule110
5800: artifact suite has been rerun for this submission.  It is that a theory-to-paper
5801: pipeline can preserve traceability by separating source evidence, deterministic
5802: gates, agent suggestions, human promotion decisions, and evidence-level
5803: boundaries, and by rejecting stronger readings whose finite certificate fields
5804: are absent.
5805: 
5806: The closing support records identify what may travel with a presentation-only
5807: submission: the primary two-page article, this technical supplement, the bounded
5808: manual theorem-obligation ledger, and the review bundle if it is uploaded exactly
5809: with matching final digests or replaced by an archive-equivalent locator.  If
5810: that external support surface is absent, the bundle-backed claims remain local
5811: path-verified records.  In all cases the theorem inventory indexes obligations
5812: only; the printed TeX statements and proofs, not the inventory, discharge the
5813: mathematical obligations of the finite-record safety theorem chain.
5814: 
